  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 137 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nA ridge continue to trek eastward Tuesday across the Central CONUS \nwith southwesterly flow and WAA in place, keeping temperatures in \nthe 50s Tuesday. Wednesday a cold front advances into the area, will \nsee compressional heating aiding in temperatures ahead of the front \nrising into the low 60s. As the front passes through the area \nwinds will be breezy and switch to the northwest. Winds of 15 to\n25 mph with gusts up to 45 mph will be possible. Precipitation \nchances will remain low despite the passage of the front. \n\nAlthough guidance still points to another system moving into the \nCentral Plains by the end of the week, uncertainties still remain. \nThe track has changed from each model run. Some of the runs have \nshown the system tracking further south as a closed low system, \nhowever the latest run as move the track further north in more of an \nopen wave pattern. The inconsistencies have led to lower confidence \non both track and strength of the system and precipitation chances. \nFor now continue to keep the potential for widespread precipitation \nin the forecast, however this may change as the week progresses and \nthe models become more in consensus with a solution on the track, \ntiming and strength of the system.",
